# T6. return: addN is one merge: model addN, {n: this activation}, header (int: x) int.
# add5 and add100 are two nodes. n is each node's own field. The frames are shared.
# [add5: 1; add100: 1; add5: 1] is 6, 101, 6. One exit_code is not that list: Entry 7.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    return: addN

add5: makeAdder 5
add100: makeAdder 100
int: a (add5: 1)
int: b (add100: 1)
int: c (add5: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 6 && b = 101 && c = 6
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
